# Open Dungeon Master (ODM) Cursor Rules

You are working on Open Dungeon Master (ODM), a D&D 5e multiplayer tabletop and AI Game Master platform.

## Crucial Reference Files
- Read `AGENTS.md` in the workspace root for complete server specs, SSH credentials, and the External Narrator protocol.
- Consult `open-dungeon-master/.opencode/skills/odm-narrator/SKILL.md` when acting as or developing the AI Dungeon Master.

## Core Rules for Coding & Pair Programming
- Stack: TypeScript 5+, Next.js 15 (App Router), React 19, Tailwind CSS, SQLite.
- Language: Russian is the primary creative/game language for stories, chat, and DM narrative. UI supports RU, EN, PL.
- Server: Production is at `root@api.iroslyakov.com` in `/opt/odm`.
- MCP Control Plane: Always test MCP changes using `scripts/test-mcp-tools-contract.mjs` and `scripts/test-mcp-narrator-control.mjs`.
- Rules Boundary: In ODM, the server owns dice, sheets, combat, and mechanics. The AI narrator never fabricates roll results or changes sheets directly without invoking the rules engine.
